course: dictionary
lesson: 1590
title: Cheaply
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Cheaply» is an adverb. It tells you how something is done or bought. Its main meaning is for a low price, without spending much money. Look at the words around it to check: «The shop sold the old bike cheaply, for only five pounds» tells you the price was low.
explain: «Cheaply» can also mean in a poor-quality way, made without care. Read the clue words closely. «The toys were cheaply made and broke on the first day» is not about the price. The word «made» and the broken toys show that the toys were not made well.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. If «for a low price» fits, you have the first meaning. If the sentence is about how something was made, the second meaning is likely. Remember that «cheaply» has more forms: «more cheaply» and «most cheaply» compare prices.
fact: «Cheaply» is an adverb, so it describes how something is done or bought.
fact: «Cheaply» means for a low price, without spending much money.
fact: «Cheaply made» means made in a poor-quality way, without care.
fact: Ships move huge loads cheaply, so most of the world's goods travel by sea.
fact: When you compare prices to find the best value, you are looking for where you can buy something most cheaply.
exercise: «The shop sold the old bike cheaply, for only five pounds.» What does cheaply mean here? | With great care | Very fast | *For a low price | Loudly
exercise: «The toys were cheaply made and broke on the first day.» What does «cheaply made» suggest? | Made by a famous artist | Made very slowly and carefully | Made from gold | *Made in a poor-quality way, without care
exercise: «Ships move huge loads cheaply.» Find and copy the adverb in this sentence. | *cheaply | huge | loads | ships
test: «A shop buys goods cheaply in large amounts and sells them for a higher price.» Why does the shop buy goods cheaply? | Because the workers like the goods | So it can give the goods away free | Because the goods are very old | *So it pays a low price and can sell for more
test: Dad says, «We live cheaply, so we can save for the holiday.» What does «live cheaply» mean? | Live in a very big house | *Spend little money on everyday things | Live with lots of noisy pets | Live in a castle by the sea
exam: Which sentence uses «cheaply» to mean in a poor-quality way? | «The chair was painted cheaply in the sun.» | «We walked cheaply along the beach.» | «The cheaply made chair was sold for a low price at the market.» | *«The cheaply made chair wobbled when I sat on it.»
